# Theme & Environment Configuration

## 1. Local Database Environment
- **Provider:** PostgreSQL
- **Connection URL:** `DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:2004@localhost:5432/sandbox_db`
- Use this connection schema context for defining backend database connections (Prisma, Drizzle, or pg pools).

## 2. Global Design Tokens (Tailwind CSS Configuration)
Apply these specific colors when generating Tailwind CSS classes, component inline designs, or theme files:

| Token Name | Hex Code | Ideal Usage / Rules |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Primary Background** | `#000000` | Pure Black. Use for core backdrops to mimic theater vibes and save OLED battery. |
| **Secondary Background** | `#121212` to `#1F1F1F` | Ultra-Dark Charcoal. Use for navbars, search inputs, and movie cards to build layer depth. |
| **Primary Text** | `#FFFFFF` | Pure White. Use strictly for prominent movie titles and active navigation links. |
| **Secondary Text** | `#9E9E9E` | Muted Gray. Use for metadata snippets (genres, release years, plot summaries). |
| **Accent Color** | Chosen Choice | Use sparingly for interactive items like the primary "Play" button, active icons, or logos. |
| **Success Indicator** | `#4CAF50` | Emerald Green. Use for badges like "98% Match" metrics or "Downloaded" visual cues. |

## 3. Brand Accent Guidelines
- When generating active interactive UI elements, align them under a distinct premium streaming identity using clear contrasting accent states. Avoid clashing the accent tones across multiple components.